# `vercel deploy` from this folder uploads every file these lines don't
# name. Unlike a Git deployment it never reads .gitignore, and its own
# defaults leave out only .env.local and .env.*.local, so without this file
# .env and .env.test, which hold secrets, would be uploaded. The env lines
# are the same as .gitignore's.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.test.example
